    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13685" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποσῐώπ-ησις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>, ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>becoming silent,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Alex.</u>
				52
			</span></i>, Herod.
				Med.
			in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Rh.Mus.</u>
				58.71
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> a rhetorical
			figure, when for emphasis, modesty, etc., the sentence is
				<i>abruptly broken off,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Quint.
				<u>Inst.</u>
				9.2.54
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Demetr.
				<u>Eloc.</u>
				103
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				264
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.1009e
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hermog.
				<u>Id.</u>
				2.7
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>breaking off</i> of friendship, <i><span class="en">
				Ptol.
				<u>Tetr.</u>
				192
			</span></i> (pl.).</div>
